'''''Nicotiana paniculata''''', the '''small-flowered tobacco''', is a species of flowering plant in the family [[Solanaceae]], native to western Peru, and introduced to the [[Canary Islands]].<ref name="817020-1" >{{cite POWO |id=817020-1 |title=''Nicotiana paniculata'' L. |access-date=3 March 2022 }}</ref><ref name="NIOPA" >{{cite web |url=https://gd.eppo.int/taxon/NIOPA |title=''Nicotiana paniculata'' (NIOPA) |author=<!--Not stated--> |date=2022 |website=EPPO Global Database |publisher=European and Mediterranean Plant Protection Organization |access-date=3 March 2022 }}</ref> It is a parent of the economically important species ''[[Nicotiana rustica]]'' (Aztec tobacco).<ref name="1_of_739_Google_Scholar_results" >{{cite journal |title=The impact of genome evolution on the allotetraploid ''Nicotiana rustica'' – an intriguing story of enhanced alkaloid production |year=2018 |last1=Sierro |first1=N. |last2=Battey |first2=J. N. D. |last3=Bovet |first3=L. |last4=Liedschulte |first4=V. |last5=Ouadi |first5=S. |last6=Thomas |first6=J. |last7=Broye |first7=H. |last8=Laparra |first8=H. |last9=Vuarnoz |first9=A. |last10=Lang |first10=G. |last11=Goepfert |first11=S. |last12=Peitsch |first12=M. C. |last13=Ivanov |first13=N. V. |journal=BMC Genomics |volume=19 |issue=1 |page=855 |doi=10.1186/s12864-018-5241-5 |pmid=30497378 |pmc=6267829 |doi-access=free }}</ref>

